/-!
# Corrected source reductions for 15.2.21--22

The source seed uses O², NI is M ∩ I, and MI is Mc ∩ I. The residual
comparison uses the literal Kc = ⟨O²(H)^Mc⟩. The actual wreath quotient
constructs normal cubic residual factors in the reducible case and proves
O₂(H) ≤ S. The earlier component-orbit alternative then proves that Kc
centralizes ZS and equals O^{3′}(Mc ∩ I). The binary-component applications
consume these results and the complete 15.2.21(2) application. The canonical
Y₁ = O^{3′}(NI) satisfies the conjugate-seed commutator relation by the
actual Omega action. The pair starts with the literal O²(K ∩ X); its
normality in MI proves K = Kc. The component consumer uses the proved
seed quotient, residual comparison and local normalizer contradiction.
ComplementExclusion completes the linear-three contradiction from the earlier
source inputs: the constructed action-kernel complement can be placed second
in a conjugate pair, so no exhaustive factor-recognition premise is needed.
TerminalExterior discharges the pair-quotient and T-irreducibility premises
of the original exterior-five exclusion using the actual wreath residual.
CubicSeeds proves O²(Y₁S) = Y₁ and |Y₁/O₂(Y₁)| = 3 for every corrected
source seed. MiddleParabolic lifts the invariant middle node of L₄(2) into
the literal Kc and puts its residual in C_M(V), retaining the S₃ quotient
after adjoining the original S. ElementaryStar uses this to exclude the
elementary-nine alternative of the original star residual in 15.2.3.
SeedAction identifies the action image of every corrected outside seed with
the nonnormal cubic residual of NI and lifts it to an actual cubic subgroup.
CyclicStar then excludes the original cyclic star alternative: the two
independent cubic images exhaust the three-rank and force C_M(V) to have
order prime to three. StarReduction leaves only the actual extraspecial
star residual of order 27. TerminalStar applies this reduction to the
binary terminal owner's seed inside the original X and literal Kc quotient.

ExtraspecialAction proves that the original S fixes the star residual center:
normalizing the nonnormal outside cubic forces a scalar sign on the full
rank-two image, and the marked Heisenberg determinant fixes its central line.
MiddleStar identifies the literal middle-seed image with this center.
SeedCentralImage then contradicts its original S₃ quotient through the
two-group kernel. ExtraspecialExclusion proves corrected 15.2.21(3) for every
outside seed. TerminalExclusion applies it to the actual binary component,
with T-irreducibility discharged by the original wreath quotient.

FullResidualSeed handles the full order-nine action image by deriving seed
containment and relative normality in the literal residual. CubicResidualSeed
proves relative normality in YY₁ in the cubic-image branch. CubicResidualActor
constructs an element of T − S normalizing that join from O₂(M ∩ Mc), using
its actual action. ResidualExclusion combines the branches into the arbitrary-seed
15.2.22 exclusion for every actual conjugate residual pair, and constructs the
pair from reducibility in its final application. ChiefPair identifies the original J(H) image in H/O₂(H) with S₃ × S₃.
PairedQuotient proves that the literal KS quotient is that paired image
when S is reducible, and supplies its actual binary terminal application.
TerminalRows excludes the natural-dual, natural-four and orthogonal-six
rows directly from the original residual rank. Together with the exterior
exclusion, it constructs the actual terminal natural-five action and
point-parabolic marking with no KS quotient premise. NaturalPair constructs
the KS pair quotient from the literal point action and closes the binary
terminal contradiction. Its final component application also discharges
relative normality and the residual placements.

MarkedWreath proves the complementary natural chief planes, their opposite
centralizer factors and the coordinate transvection calculations. ChiefMarking
transports them to the original vectors and actors. ChiefCoordinates supplies
the natural wreath action on each original noncentral chief factor, with
kernel O₂(H). MarkedAssembly uses the best-offender transvections and source
Thompson equality to identify the literal KS with the product of the original
marked centralizers. Every t in T − S exchanges their residuals. Together with
the orbit identities this completes all clauses of15.2.21(1). MarkedResiduals
proves the intrinsic cubic core quotients and relative normality of those
residuals. MarkedExclusion constructs the actual marked ResidualPair and
applies15.2.22 to the original K₂, with no pair premise. Its complete15.2.21(1)
constructor also chooses a noncentral chief factor, so no coordinate or split
input remains.
The genuine earlier source inputs remain for final plane-uniqueness
assembly to discharge. The legacy
SmallActions declarations are preserved and are not used as source theorems.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
printed pp.1113--1117; refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/
